english_question:
A cube is unfolded as shown in the figure. The following conclusions are made about the original cube: The correct conclusion numbers are ______. (List all the figures that meet the requirements) 
① AB ⊥ EF; 
② The angle between AB and CM is 60°; 
③ EF and MN are skew lines; 
④ MN ∥ CD.

Which of the following statements are correct (__):
(1) As shown in Figure (a), a ruler and a set square can be used to measure the diameter of a circular workpiece;
(2) As shown in Figure (b), a try square can be used to check if a workpiece is semicircular;
(3) As shown in Figure (c), using a T-square twice (the line CD being the perpendicular bisector of segment AB) can locate the center of a circular workpiece;
(4) As shown in Figure (d), the angle between the zero mark line of a clinometer and the plumb line equals the angle of elevation when looking from point P to point A.
Options:
(A) 1 correct statement
(B) 2 correct statements
(C) 3 correct statements
(D) 4 correct statements
